LRC negation-involution fixed points and AP tight-witness structure
monad-explorer-S700, extending S679 to even n

===== n = 5  (parity: odd) =====
  Fix(sigma_n)  (a = -a mod n) : [0]   [#=1]
  Shell modulus C=2n-1 = 9 (odd always); Fix(sigma_C) = [0] [#=1]
  AP_n = [1, 2, 3, 4]
  AP tight j (j/n simultaneously >= 1/n) : [1, 2, 3, 4]   [#=4]
  units mod n (gcd(j,n)=1)               : [1, 2, 3, 4]   [phi(n)=4]
  tight == units ?  True
  non-tight j (gcd>1): []
  negation on tight times: pairs [(1, 4), (2, 3)]; self-fixed tight times: []

